title the witnesses nobody ran -- 26 Glow proofs get a clock, and one of them was already red
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure lane.
think ListAgents answered "No reachable agents" at the open, so no peer to name before moving a file. The cold roster ran 79 guards, 78 green, one red -- declared_ceiling, which my own previous lap had already read and surfaced. Repeating that suggestion a second time is the twice-repeated unasked suggestion the voice names as a red, so I read it for a sharper root instead of pressing it.
think The rota computed row 3 -- N is git rev-list --count HEAD at 3643, and 3643 mod 5 is 3. My previous recorded row was 4, so this is a backward jump rather than a repeat and no hand advance was owed. Water, Venus, care and flow, sense of taste: read up close, run the actual witness. The fixed seat is the happy zone and the thin edge, whose closing question is what the zone rewards -- "witnesses cheap enough to actually run; a check nobody can afford stops being a check." The lap turned out to be exactly that sentence twice over.
think The charter active-designing/20260827-174816 numbers its own remaining plan, and item 1 is "the roster hears the language" -- 89 Glow witnesses, zero rostered, six without a caller, called the cheapest fix on the list. Everything else in that charter has landed except the deep debride, which is custody gate %5. So item 1 was the lane's crux and it was already written down.
think My first measurement was wrong and the second look corrected it in public. Counting files that NAME a witness gave 10 uncalled, because a prose mention in a design note is not a caller. Counting only tracked runners -- .rish, .sh, .rye -- and then subtracting the standing roster's own rows gave the honest 26.
obs Running all 26 by hand is the finding. Twenty-four green, one red, and one that looked red only because my 120s cap cut it off. tools/g/glow_g5_nock_family_notes_witness.rish asserted on active-designing/20260720-033200_stoa98-g5-nock-second-backend-family-notes.md, which folded to active-designing/yonder/date/20260720/ -- the assert had been reading a missing file rather than a Nock fact, and no clock existed to say so. The resolver named the new home; one substitution in a living file closed it.
obs active-designing/docs/glow/glow_book_anchor_witness.rish was green and unaffordable. Its direction-two reading ran one recursive grep over glow/ per anchor -- 34 greps, 271s measured -- for a number it reports rather than gates. Collecting the referenced anchors once into a temp file and asking the set with grep -qxF gives the identical answer in 8.4s, and the whole witness fell 280s to 25s. Proven both ways before installing: identical zero orphans on the real tree, and a planted g-plantedghost anchor reported by name in a throwaway pen.
obs The completeness half was already built, which is why this lap built no second loom. tools/fixtures/witness_reach_scan.sh traces reachability tree-wide and gates unreached under a ceiling that only falls. Rostering the choir moved 27 witnesses into cadence, so the reading fell 1,140 to 1,113 and the ceiling fell 1,154 to 1,113 with no slack left; wholly_unreached fell 221 to 220 and its ceiling followed. A new Glow witness that nothing runs now raises unreached above a ceiling sitting exactly on the reading, which is the recurrence guard, so a second bijection inside the choir would have been one more loom watching one lantern.
obs No REDS row booked, and the check is why. The sharper root I found behind declared_ceiling -- that the scan reads digits, so tools/l/chatgpt-mind.sh:23's MAX_PROMPT_BYTES, a prompt budget that merely equals 24,576, is counted as a copy of the living-pin law -- is already written in REDS %295, in better words than mine, OPEN and gated on Keaton's word with three named shapes. Fetch-before-book gave 329 as next free and I spent it on nothing.
obs One detail %295 does not carry, left here rather than editing a row that is never edited: a second reading inside the same scan is already over and unreachable. tools/fixtures/declared_ceiling_scan.sh exits at line 393 with verdict=law_number_copied, so the recitation check at line 397 never runs, and law_copies_reciting reads 9 against law_recite_ceiling=6. Two of those nine are the same chatgpt-mind lines, so one root feeds both gates and whichever shape closes %295 should be measured against both numbers rather than the first.
obs The 201 stale tools/gen/chapter citations my previous lap handed forward measure as zero living work. All 311 files citing tools/gen/chapter/equinox carry one-clock stamps in their own basenames, which makes every one of them dated testimony -- resolved rather than rewritten. The room fold repointed what was living before it shipped.
